IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bnra-types`

-- Business Names Registration Act 2014, Part 2, ss 25 to 31: rectification of the
-- register, copies, the electronic transaction system, the transitional contact
-- address, and the disability of persons in default.
-- Source: source/BNRA2014.txt lines 1180 to 1458.

§ `Part 2 -- Registration: the register and defaults`

§§ `25. Rectification by General Division of High Court`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 25(1)"
GIVEN c IS A `Court Rectification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the General Division of the High Court may direct the Registrar to rectify the register` IF
        c's `evidence has been adduced before the General Division of the High Court by an applicant`
    AND c's `a particular recorded in the register appears erroneous or defective as a result of that evidence`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 25(2)"
GIVEN `the Registrar has received an order of the General Division of the High Court under section 25(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must rectify the register accordingly` IF
    `the Registrar has received an order of the General Division of the High Court under section 25(1)`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 25(3)"
GIVEN c IS A `Court Rectification Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant must file a fresh document with a copy of the order and of the application` IF
    c's `the order requires a fresh document showing the rectification to be filed`

§§ `26. Rectification by Registrar on application`

-- 26(1) lets a registered person or authorised representative notify an error; 26(2) lets
-- the Registrar rectify a typographical or clerical error in a document relating to the
-- person's particulars, or an unintended, non-prejudicial error in filing; 26(3) forbids
-- expunging a document.  26(4) makes the Registrar's decision final: inert.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 26(1), (2)(a) and (b), (3)"
GIVEN n IS A `Rectification Notice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may rectify the register on the notice` IF
        n's `the notice is lodged by a registered person or the person's authorised representative`
    AND (   (    n's `the notice is of an error in a document relating to the person's particulars filed or lodged with the Registrar`
             AND n's `the error is typographical or clerical in nature`)
         OR (    n's `the notice is of an error in the filing or lodgment of a document relating to the person`
             AND n's `the error is, in the Registrar's opinion, unintended and does not prejudice any person`))
    AND NOT n's `rectifying the register would expunge a document from the register`

§§ `27. Rectification or updating on Registrar's initiative`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 27(1)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS A `Registrar Initiative Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may rectify or update on the Registrar's own initiative` IF
        r's `the Registrar is satisfied there is a defect or error arising from a grammatical, typographical or similar mistake`
     OR r's `there is evidence of a conflict between the person's particulars and other information in the register or information from a prescribed body`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 27(2)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN r IS A `Registrar Initiative Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice requirement of section 27(2) is met` IF
        r's `the circumstances are ones in which written notice is not required`
     OR (    r's `the Registrar gave written notice of the intention to rectify or update`
         AND r's `the number of days the notice allowed for a written objection` AT LEAST 30)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 27(3), (4) and (5)"
GIVEN r IS A `Registrar Initiative Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an objection stops the Registrar from rectifying or updating` IF
        r's `a written objection was delivered by the date specified`
    AND NOT r's `the Registrar is satisfied that the objection is frivolous or vexatious or has been withdrawn`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 27(1), (2), (4) and (5)"
GIVEN r IS A `Registrar Initiative Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` IF
        `the Registrar may rectify or update on the Registrar's own initiative` r
    AND `the notice requirement of section 27(2) is met` r
    AND NOT `an objection stops the Registrar from rectifying or updating` r

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 27(7)"
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that there is an error or defect in particulars or a document in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may request the registered person to take steps to rectify the error or defect` IF
    `the Registrar is satisfied that there is an error or defect in particulars or a document in the register`

-- 27(6): the Registrar may add a notation to the register about an error or defect, and
-- remove it when it serves no useful purpose: a power with no condition, inert.

§§ `28. Request for copy of notice of registration, etc.`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 28(1), (3) and (4)"
GIVEN c IS A `Copy Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may require a copy or extract to be given or certified` IF
        c's `the person has paid the fees prescribed`
    AND NOT c's `the document is prescribed as an excluded document`
    AND NOT c's `the document forms part of the register and has been destroyed under section 38`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 28(2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Copy Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certified copy or extract is admissible in evidence as of equal validity with the original` IF
    c's `the copy or extract is certified by the Registrar to be a true copy or extract`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 28(5)(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN c IS A `Copy Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entry is excluded from the reference to a document in section 28(1)` IF
        c's `the document was submitted on the electronic transaction system on or after the commencement of section 24 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024`
    AND c's `the entry is a means of notification provided for section 28A(1)(b) of the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004, an individual's date of birth, or other prescribed information`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 28(6)"
GIVEN c IS A `Copy Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must exclude the residential address from every copy or extract` IF
        c's `the document was submitted on the electronic transaction system on or after the commencement of section 24 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024`
    AND c's `the entry is an individual's residential address`

§§ `29. Electronic transaction system`

-- 29(1) lets the Registrar require or permit transactions and issue documents through the
-- electronic transaction system, and 29(4) defines "transaction": powers and a definition
-- with no condition, inert.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 29(2)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Earlier Time Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may cause the system and the register to reflect the earlier date and time` IF
    e's `the Registrar is satisfied that a transaction should be treated as having been carried out at an earlier date and time`

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 29(3)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Earlier Time Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must keep a record of the alteration` IF
    e's `the Registrar is satisfied that a transaction should be treated as having been carried out at an earlier date and time`

§§ `30. Transitional provision for contact address`

-- 30(1) and (2): until notice of a change of contact address is lodged under an ACRA
-- administered Act on or after the commencement date, the contact address is the alternate
-- address the individual maintained with the Registrar or, if none, the residential address.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 30(1) and (2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Contact Address Transition Facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the individual's contact address for the purposes of the Act` MEANS
    IF c's `notice of a change of the contact address has been lodged under an ACRA administered Act on or after the commencement date`
    THEN c's `the contact address lodged`
    ELSE (IF c's `the individual maintained an alternate address with the Registrar immediately before the commencement date`
          THEN c's `the alternate address`
          ELSE c's `the individual's residential address`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 30(3)"
`the transitional contact address is deemed a particular registered for the purposes of section 20(1)` MEANS TRUE

-- 30(4) defines "commencement date": inert.

§§ `31. Disability of persons in default`

-- 31(2): the defaulter may not enforce by action any right under a contract made at a time
-- when (a) it was not registered under the name, (b) its registration had been cancelled or
-- had ceased and had not been restored, or (c) it was in breach of s 19(1) or 20(1) or (3).
-- 31(3): the (b) disability lifts if the registration is restored.  31(7): the defaulter may
-- still enforce, by counterclaim, set-off or otherwise, rights against a party who has
-- sued it on the contract.

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 31(1) and (2)(a), (b), (c) and (3)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disability in section 31(2) attaches to the contract` IF
        d's `the person is required to be registered`
    AND (   d's `the contract was made when the person carried on business under the name without being registered under it`
         OR (    (   d's `the contract was made when the registration under the name had been cancelled and not restored`
                  OR d's `the contract was made when the registration under the name had ceased and not restored`)
             AND NOT d's `the registration was later restored under section 24`)
         OR d's `the contract was made when the person was in breach of section 19(1) or 20(1) or (3)`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 31(2) and (7)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defaulter may not enforce the right` IF
        `the disability in section 31(2) attaches to the contract` d
    AND NOT (    d's `another party has commenced an action to enforce that party's rights under the contract`
             AND d's `the person seeks to enforce a right against that party, by counterclaim, set-off or otherwise, in respect of the contract`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 31(4) and (5)(a) and (b)"
GIVEN d IS A `Disability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may grant relief against the disability` IF
        d's `the person has applied to the court for relief`
    AND (   d's `the court is satisfied that the default was accidental or due to inadvertence or some other sufficient reason`
         OR d's `the court is satisfied that on other grounds it is just and equitable to grant relief`)

@ref "Business Names Registration Act 2014, s 31(6)"
`section 31 affects the rights of any other party against the defaulter in respect of the contract` MEANS FALSE

-- 31(8) defines "court": inert.
